.claude-hooks/

# atomic-write temp from router_eac_calibrate.py / router_shared_upweight.py
# (.tmp + os.replace pattern that breaks hardlinks). Should never be staged.
*.eac_write_tmp

# imatrix.dat ARCHIVAL EXCEPTION:
# imatrix files MUST be kept WITH their quants when published, but we don't
# want them in this repo (which holds code, not artifacts).

# generated code-graph output (regenerable)
graphify-out/

# aime_100 lm-eval task yaml: GENERATED per host, because dataset_kwargs.data_files
# must be an ABSOLUTE path (HF datasets resolves relative paths against CWD and
# lm-eval does not chdir to the task dir). Committing one host's copy guarantees a
# stale pointer on every other host. The DATA (aime_100.jsonl) and the build report
# ARE committed and are byte-identical across hosts.
# Materialise with: python eval/build_aime100_dataset.py --yaml-only
eval/lm_eval_tasks/aime100_chat/aime100_chat.yaml

# RL / replay PROMPT POOLS: the BUILDERS are committed, the built pools are not.
#   scripts/build_lcb_rl_pool.py       -> eval/lcb/lcb_rl_pool.jsonl
#   scripts/build_gepo_replay_pool.py  -> eval/replay/gepo_replay_pool.jsonl
#
# This repo is PUBLIC. gepo_replay_pool.jsonl embeds 250 GPQA questions together
# with their correct answers in plaintext. GPQA is a GATED dataset that ships a
# canary string precisely so its questions do not end up in web crawls and leak
# into future pretraining sets — publishing them here would contaminate GPQA for
# everyone, not just for us, and it is not ours to publish. MBPP (CC-BY-4.0) is
# already public and carries no such constraint, but the pool is one file.
#
# Nothing is lost: the builders are deterministic (fixed seed, hash-pinned dataset
# snapshots) and print their own holdout provenance, so anyone with legitimate
# GPQA access reproduces the pool byte-for-byte from committed code.
eval/lcb/lcb_rl_pool.jsonl
eval/replay/gepo_replay_pool.jsonl
